WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.500
Which parts of an AI workflow should be

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.260
fixed in code, and which should the model decide?

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.680
Torok is the agent harness in the Canary Desk suite.

4
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.160
Built as a Go library, it supplies the

5
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.820
software around a model: tools, workflow execution, and saved progress.

6
00:00:17.933 --> 00:00:21.153
Imagine asking it to summarize two project updates.

7
00:00:21.813 --> 00:00:24.233
Code sets the required steps: load the reports,

8
00:00:24.453 --> 00:00:27.293
produce a brief, check it, and ask for review.

9
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.360
Inside the drafting step, the work is agentic:

10
00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.300
the model chooses what to investigate.

11
00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:37.080
It can read a report, compare the findings, or call an allowed tool.

12
00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:39.993
Look inside a single tool call.

13
00:00:40.533 --> 00:00:42.973
The model decides to calculate five minus two.

14
00:00:43.673 --> 00:00:45.053
Ordinary code returns three.

15
00:00:45.413 --> 00:00:47.873
The model explains what those three mean.

16
00:00:48.967 --> 00:00:51.287
Code checks required fields and counts.

17
00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:55.507
A brief reporting zero failures conflicts with the two in the evidence.

18
00:00:56.047 --> 00:00:58.187
The check rejects it; the model revises.

19
00:00:59.007 --> 00:00:59.927
Retries have limits.

20
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:05.260
Inside Desk, Torok’s resident receives messages and scheduled work.

21
00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:07.200
Workflows define the steps.

22
00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.640
Agents run the model and tool loop.

23
00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:13.700
A shared runtime coordinates execution, limits, and recovery.

24
00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:17.700
State lives in two local SQLite databases.

25
00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:21.300
The service database stores the inbox, schedules, and memory.

26
00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:25.240
The episodes database stores runs, checkpoints, events, and

27
00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:28.000
conversations, so work can resume from saved results.

28
00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:35.727
So codify obligations: data access, calculations, checks, permissions, and stopping.

29
00:01:36.207 --> 00:01:41.107
Use agents for interpretation, investigation, and drafting within that structure.

30
00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.720
The workflow defines what must happen.

31
00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.780
The agent decides how to reason within it.

32
00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.480
Torok carries the work between the two.
